      "source": "operator",
      "author": "Dennis",
      "authorId": "__DEV_USER__",
      "text": "The Codex SDK is so limited compared to Claude. With Claude, we have hooks, middlewares, system prompts. There's so much more that we can accomplish with Claude that we can't with Codex. What I'm thinking is: can we learn from Claude's SDK to see how they do it with their CLI, and to see if maybe we can create our own custom wrapper that forks from the Codex official SDK that can give us way more options and configuration with Codex?",
      "kind": "chat",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-13T22:43:31.771896+00:00"
    },
    {
